@@@!atrep

@@/ at-html: a syntax mapper between a useful subset of HTML and
@@/ atrep. Each sim corresponds to one HTML element; the html
@@/ exomorphosis and the engine-side HTML endomorphosis are
@@/ inverses over the canonical subset. Inline and block code map
@@/ to the core enlexis forms, images to enmedia. Serves as the
@@/ standard-library base dialektos: at-markdown inherits from it.

@=== blockquote
@>
grammata
>@
@"block quotation (blockquote element)"@
===@

@=== division
@_
grammata
_@
@"generic block container (div element; genoses map to class)"@
===@

@=== emphasis
@/ grammata /@
@"emphasis (em element)"@
===@

@=== link
@>< grammata ><@
@"hyperlink; the grammata is the displayed URL"@
@""
The visible-URL link (an anchor whose text is its target, or
none). Hidden-href links (display text distinct from the URL)
are deferred pending F9; the endomorphosis meanwhile projects
them as prose text with the visible URL beside it.
""@
===@

@=== heading-1
@# grammata #@
@"level-1 heading (h1 element); flat, does not nest content"@
===@

@=== heading-2
@## grammata ##@
@"level-2 heading (h2 element)"@
===@

@=== heading-3
@### grammata ###@
@"level-3 heading (h3 element)"@
===@

@=== heading-4
@#### grammata ####@
@"level-4 heading (h4 element)"@
===@

@=== heading-5
@##### grammata #####@
@"level-5 heading (h5 element)"@
===@

@=== heading-6
@###### grammata ######@
@"level-6 heading (h6 element)"@
===@

@=== ordered-item
@.(taxis)
grammata
.@
@"ordered list item (li element with a value)"@
===@

@=== ordered-list
@..
grammata
..@
@"ordered list (ol element)"@
===@

@=== span
@, grammata ,@
@"generic inline container (span element; genoses map to class)"@
===@

@=== strong
@! grammata !@
@"strong emphasis (strong element)"@
===@

@=== verse
@~[(taxis)] [lemma]
stichos
~@ [hypograph]
@"line-structured block (verse, or any lined content)"@
===@

@=== unordered-item
@-
grammata
-@
@"unordered list item (li element)"@
===@

@=== unordered-list
@--
grammata
--@
@"unordered list (ul element)"@
===@
